    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "The quote you wrote sounds a bit too \"salesy\" for a guy like Vance. He’s a data guy; if I tell him we're \"betting on innovation\" when the report literally says they won't have the liquidity to survive the transition, he's going to call my bluff immediately.\n\nLet's be more aggressive with the framing. If he asks directly, \"This report says mid-sized firms will see a 15% drop in net revenue due to 4C, how do you respond to that?\", I can't just say the report is \"conservative.\" I need to be able to tell him that the report is actually flawed or that the negative impact is a temporary, manageable spike that doesn't reflect the reality of the math. \n\nGive me a way to tell him that the 15% figure is essentially a worst-case scenario that doesn't account for the actual market incentives in the bill. I need a way to pivot so he believes the downside is negligible or overstated.",
